From 56132fce24a3ffaa7f25769e1be785c9da2d3241 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ericek111 <erik.brocko@letemsvetemapplem.eu>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 13:13:27 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 31/47] translator: split vector loads over GEP-indexed slots
 of another same-width type

Apple's GL compiler addresses a GLSL ivec3 at the start of a uniform block
as getelementptr float and loads it as <3 x i32>. vec_scalar_merge only
scalarized components whose uses share one element type, so the emitter
failed (reinterpret load bit width mismatch Float vs <3 x i32>) and
Minecraft's terrain vertex shader never got a pipeline: AppleMetalGL ran
it on the CPU (SW vertex processing). Such components now split into slot
loads/stores with a per-lane bitcast; the plain reinterpret mix without a
GEP stays untouched. Minecraft 26.3: 2 -> 22 fps.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
